    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Two-Number Calculator\n\nA retro pixel-style calculator that performs basic arithmetic on two numbers. Fully offline, no dependencies.\n\n## Features\n\n- Two number inputs (left and right) with support for negative values\n- Operation selector: add, subtract, multiply, divide\n- Displays numeric result or `Error` for invalid inputs\n- Rejects empty inputs, non-finite numbers, and division by zero\n- Pixel-art aesthetic with monospace font and blocky borders\n- Keyboard accessible with visible focus states\n- Responsive design works from 360px wide\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter numbers in the **Left Number** and **Right Number** fields.\n3. Choose an operation from the dropdown.\n4. Click **Calculate** (or press Enter while focused on the button).\n5. The result appears below. If inputs are invalid, `Error` is shown.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- Empty fields → `Error`\n- Non-numeric or infinite values → `Error`\n- Division by zero → `Error`\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` — Complete self-contained app (HTML, CSS, JS inline)\n- `README.md` — This file\n\n## License\n\nMIT",
